<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <!-- NOT PublishSingleFile — the app runs via `dotnet TakOne.MigrationFixer.dll`
         so it doesn't need to be a single-file executable. PublishSingleFile=true
         requires UseAppHost=true, which conflicts with the /p:UseAppHost=false
         flag the Dockerfile uses for all publish steps. -->
    <SelfContained>false</SelfContained>
    <!-- Suppress nullable warnings — this is a tiny utility, not a production app. -->
    <NoWarn>CS8600;CS8603;CS8604;CS8625</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Same SqlClient version the main app uses — shared framework provides the rest.
         (Was 6.0.1 — drifted from Infrastructure's 6.1.7; realigned.) -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Data.SqlClient" Version="6.1.7" />

    <!--
      Direct, explicit override of SqlClient's TRANSITIVE dependency
      System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs.

      WHY: SqlClient 6.x references the Pkcs 9.x line (9.0.0 from 6.0.1,
      9.0.11 from 6.1.7) — and the ENTIRE 9.x line carries known
      advisories (GHSA-2fmv-rv2c-59x7 moderate + GHSA-846f-f764-76mx
      high), never to be patched: .NET 9 is EOL. NuGet's audit
      (elevated to error by the repo-wide TreatWarningsAsErrors policy)
      therefore fails this project's restore with NU1902/NU1903 —
      which broke the Docker image build (the Dockerfile publishes this
      project separately; it is NOT part of TakOne.slnx, so solution
      builds never surfaced it).

      The MAIN APP does not hit this only because its larger graph
      (WolverineFx.SqlServer / Weasel.SqlServer → Pkcs 10.0.13) floats
      the version up. This project has no such float, so the fix is the
      documented NuGet remedy for vulnerable transitive packages: a
      DIRECT reference to the patched version. Direct references win
      over transitive ones, resolving the graph to 10.0.14 — the same
      10.0.14 line the rest of the repo (EF Core / ASP.NET / Extensions)
      standardizes on.

      KEEP THIS PIN when bumping SqlClient: only remove it if SqlClient
      itself starts referencing a patched (10.x) Pkcs, or if a
      dedicated override mechanism replaces it. Re-check on every
      SqlClient bump.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs" Version="10.0.14" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
